## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is the resale value of a marquise diamond?

Natural marquise diamonds resell for 40–50% of original retail price through reputable channels. Lab marquise diamonds resell for 10–20% of retail. Both figures assume GIA or IGI certification. Uncertified stones recover less. The channel matters too — local jewelers offer 25–35%, while online auctions recover 45–55% for natural stones.

### Do marquise diamonds hold their value better than round diamonds?

No. Round brilliant natural diamonds recover 7–12 percentage points more at resale than marquise at equivalent quality and cert. Round has a larger buyer pool and deeper secondary market liquidity. Marquise pays a Fancy Shape Tax at resale due to its narrower buyer demand.

### Why do lab marquise diamonds have such low resale value?

Lab diamonds have unlimited supply. Retail prices fall every single year as production efficiency improves. A resale buyer can buy a new [lab-grown marquise](/lab-grown-marquise-diamond) at current retail. That retail may already be lower than what you paid. Dealers offer 10–20% of original retail. New lab retail minus dealer margin is all the math they need.

### How can I get more money when selling my marquise diamond?

Four levers improve resale recovery. First: get a GIA certificate before selling — $100–150 in fees returns $300–600 in higher offers. Second: sell through online platforms like Worthy.com rather than a local jeweler. Third: preserve both tips — chipped marquise tips cost 15–25% of the offer. Fourth: sell natural stones during strong market conditions, and sell lab stones sooner rather than later.

### Does the marquise length-to-width ratio affect resale value?

Yes. [Marquise stones](/marquise-cut-diamond) with L/W ratios between 1.85:1 and 2.00:1 have the strongest resale demand. Extreme ratios face additional buyer resistance — very narrow (2.2:1+) or very wide (1.6:1 or less). Dealers and private buyers want the classic elongated shape. Extreme variations are harder to place.

### Is a GIA certificate necessary to sell a marquise diamond?

Not strictly required, but highly recommended. A GIA certificate removes re-grading risk for buyers. That risk elimination translates into higher offers. An uncertified 1ct natural marquise may get 25–35% of retail. The same stone with GIA gets 40–50%. The certification fee ($100–150) always comes back in a higher offer.

### What is the best platform to sell a marquise diamond?

Online auction platforms like Worthy.com generate competitive bids from multiple dealers. They recover 5–15 percentage points more than a single local jeweler offer. For private sale, I Do Now I Don't is an established dedicated marketplace. Large natural stones (2ct+) should be quoted through Heritage Auctions or Sotheby's for best recovery.

### Should I buy a marquise engagement ring knowing resale value is lower?

Yes — if you're buying it to wear, not to invest. A [marquise diamond engagement ring](/marquise-diamond-engagement-ring) offers more face-up area per carat than round. The finger-slimming visual is real. The vintage character is distinctive. Those benefits are real. The resale discount is also real. Buy the shape you love, and don't buy any diamond expecting to profit at resale.

### How does the bowtie effect affect marquise resale value?

A visible bowtie adds 5–15% additional discount at resale on top of the base fancy shape penalty. Dealers spot bowties immediately. A severe bowtie is a known cut defect — it's priced accordingly. If you're selling a [marquise](/marquise-cut-diamond) with a notable bowtie, expect offers below the averages in this guide.

### What happens to lab diamond resale value over time?

It falls. Lab diamond retail prices have been declining 10–30% annually in many carat ranges. As retail falls, resale offers follow. A lab marquise you bought 24 months ago for $2,500 may cost $1,400 new today. A dealer won't pay you more than current new retail minus their margin. Sell lab diamonds sooner rather than later if resale matters.

### How much does the setting affect marquise diamond resale value?

Platinum settings add $100–300 in scrap value. 14k gold settings add $75–200. The stone is the primary value driver. Complete [marquise engagement rings](/marquise-diamond-engagement-ring) often attract private buyers who want the full piece. That can recover 10–20% more than selling the loose stone.

### Is a marquise diamond a good investment?

No diamond is a reliable investment for most retail buyers. Natural marquise retains value better than lab. But even the best-case natural resale at 50–60% of retail is a significant loss from what you paid. Diamonds are jewelry, not financial instruments. Buy them to wear. Choose marquise for the shape, not the exit strategy.

### What is the resale difference between a marquise solitaire and a marquise halo ring?

The center stone drives resale value in both cases. A solitaire shows the center stone directly — easy to appraise and resell loose. A halo creates a larger visual but often uses a smaller center (0.5–0.75ct instead of 1ct). Smaller centers have lower resale demand. For resale, solitaires with larger center stones generally recover more than halos at the same total retail price.
